            <ArticleTitle>High apolipoprotein B with low high-density lipoprotein cholesterol and normal plasma triglycerides and cholesterol.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>792-3, A8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Increased numbers of small, dense low-density lipoprotein particles may be present in patients with low high-density lipoprotein cholesterol and normal plasma triglycerides and cholesterol. Measurment of apolipoprotein B is the key to diagnosis and such patients should be considered for statin therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
